course: dictionary
lesson: 15097
title: A word from a game
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one game or one place. Rounders is a game played in the UK and Ireland. If you do not know it, the sentences around it give clues. «We play rounders in PE every summer.» PE is a lesson about sport, and summer is a time for outdoor games, so rounders must be a game.
explain: «Mia hit the ball hard and ran to the first post.» Hitting a ball and running to posts is what players do in rounders. Rounders is a bit like baseball, so if you know baseball, you already know some of the ideas.
explain: «Tom scored a rounder by running round all four posts.» A rounder is a point won by running all the way round the four posts. Check your idea by putting it into the sentence: "Tom scored a point by running round all four posts" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Rounders is a noun, a name for a game.
fact: Rounders is a bat-and-ball game played in the UK and Ireland.
fact: In rounders, players hit a ball and run around four posts.
fact: Rounders is a bit like baseball in the USA and softball.
fact: Phrases to know: «play rounders», «score a rounder», «rounders bat», «half a rounder».
exercise: «We play rounders in PE every summer.» What kind of thing is rounders? | *A bat-and-ball game, a bit like baseball | A kind of bread | A swimming race
exercise: «Mia hit the ball hard and ran to the first post.» What do players in rounders do with the ball? | Kick it into a net | *Hit it with a bat | Throw it into a hoop | Catch it in a basket
exercise: «Tom scored a rounder by running round all four posts.» What does «score a rounder» mean? | Hit the ball high into the sky | Sing a song with your team | *Get a point by running round all four posts | Stop the ball with your hands
test: «Lena picked up the rounders bat and got ready to hit.» What is a rounders bat for? | *Hitting the ball | Catching fish | Holding a drink | Digging holes
test: Where is rounders played? | On the moon | In the desert only | *In the UK and Ireland | On ice rinks
exam: Ella's team cheered when she scored a rounder. What did Ella do? | Gave the ball to the coach | Stopped the ball with her hands | *Ran round all four posts | Sat down to rest
